ficial Court opinion was verified.","status":"decided"}],"case_status":"decided","dek":"The SEC seeks to impose civil penalties without a jury. Jarkesy argues the Seventh Amendment requires a jury for such claims.","dek_sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 134, lines 21-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 134, lines 21-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 152, lines 31-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 152, lines 31-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 25-31","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 25-31"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 31-35","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 31-35"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 93, lines 45-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 93, lines 45-17"}],"maturity":"post_opinion","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2023","official_disposition_urls":["https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/603us1r50_7kh7.pdf"],"official_docket_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/docket/docketfiles/html/public/22-859.html","primary_docket":"22-859","revisions":[{"correction_note":"Rewritten to the concise citizen-facing editorial standard.","created_at":"2026-08-30T16:17:28.451636Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":1}],"schema_version":"1.0","sections":[{"heading":"What this case is about","paragraphs":["The dispute centers on whether the SEC can adjudicate fraud claims and impose civil penalties without a jury trial. The SEC argues Congress authorized agencies to conduct such adjudications. Jarkesy contends the Seventh Amendment guarantees a jury for these claims."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 134, lines 21-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 134, lines 21-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 152, lines 31-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 152, lines 31-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 25-31","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 25-31"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 31-35","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 31-35"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 93, lines 45-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 93, lines 45-17"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on November 29, 2023."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 141, lines 11-15","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2023/22-859_h280.pdf","page_label":"file page 141, lines 11-15"},{"evidence_type":"Tra